    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Turkic steppe state between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, ruled jointly by a sacral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> and a military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bek">bek</a>.</li><li>It held back Arab expansion north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and taxed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> trade linking the Islamic world to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-europe">Northern Europe</a>.</li><li>Its ruling elite famously converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>'s campaign of the 960s brought the khaganate down.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Byzantine emperor Constantine V married the Khazar princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tzitzak">Tzitzak</a>, and their son reigned as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leo-iv-the-khazar">Leo IV</a>, known as 'the Khazar'.</p></aside>
    </section>

